  "description_blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This Jumper Shunt is a specialized reset tool designed for the CyberBrick programmable hardware core board. It consists of a plastic cap containing an internal metal conductor, which enables hardware-level system recovery and debugging by physically short-circuiting specific pins on the core board. It serves as an essential accessory for in-depth device maintenance and troubleshooting."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Application: Manually restore the core board to factory settings"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "1. Remove the multi-function core board from the expansion shield. 2. Place the Jumper Shunt over Pin 1 and Pin 2 on the multi-function core board. 3. Plug the Type-C cable into the multi-function core board and a power supply. 4. Wait for 5 seconds until the LED indicator on the multi-function core board flashes purple, which means the restore is complete. 5. Open the CyberBrick mobile app or the desktop app, reconnect your device, and upload your project."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Important Notices"
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "The Jumper Shunt is to be used only when resetting the core board. After resetting, be sure to remove the Jumper Shunt and store it properly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "Keep the device out of reach of children to prevent choking hazards."
    }
  ],
  "description_html": "<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<div class=\"pct_t-p\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\" style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 24px; text-align: left;\">Introduction</h2>\n<!---红字文本替换---->\n<p class=\"pct_p\" style=\"text-align: left;\">This Jumper Shunt is a specialized reset tool designed for the CyberBrick programmable hardware core board. It consists of a plastic cap containing an internal metal conductor, which enables hardware-level system recovery and debugging by physically short-circuiting specific pins on the core board. It serves as an essential accessory for in-depth device maintenance and troubleshooting.</p>\n<!--Application: Manually restore the core board to factory settings -->\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<div class=\"pct_t-p\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\" style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 24px; text-align: left;\">Application: Manually restore the core board to factory settings</h2>\n<p class=\"pct_p\" style=\"text-align: left; margin-bottom: -10px;\">1. Remove the multi-function core board from the expansion shield.<br/>2. Place the Jumper Shunt over Pin 1 and Pin 2 on the multi-function core board.<br/>3. Plug the Type-C cable into the multi-function core board and a power supply.<br/>4. Wait for 5 seconds until the LED indicator on the multi-function core board flashes purple, which means the restore is complete.<br/>5. Open the CyberBrick mobile app or the desktop app, reconnect your device, and upload your project.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!--视频展示-->\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_ic\">\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0px;\"><video autoplay=\"autoplay\" class=\"product-desc-lazy-media product-desc-lazy-media--video bg-bbl-white animate-pulse aspect-video max-h-[400px]\" controls=\"controls\" data-lazy=\"false\" data-mce-=\"\" data-src=\"https://store.bblcdn.com/s1/default/c4c671dd198e46f3931fed3f4ab82710/Easy-Grip_Jumper_Shunt.mp4\" height=\"150\" loop=\"loop\" muted=\"\" playsinline=\"\" poster=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMjQiIGhlaWdodD0iMjQiIHZpZXdCb3g9IjAgMCAyNCAyNCIgZmlsbD0ibm9uZSIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj4KPHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjI0IiBoZWlnaHQ9IjI0IiBmaWxsPSIjRkZGRkZGIi8+Cjwvc3ZnPgo=\" style=\"width: 100%;\" width=\"300\"></video></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<div class=\"pct_t-p\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\" style=\"margin-top: 20px; font-size: 24px; text-align: left;\">Important Notices</h2>\n<!---红字文本替换---->\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"pct_p\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The Jumper Shunt is to be used only when resetting the core board. After resetting, be sure to remove the Jumper Shunt and store it properly.</li>\n<li class=\"pct_p\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Keep the device out of reach of children to prevent choking hazards.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "This Jumper Shunt is a specialized reset tool designed for the CyberBrick programmable hardware core board. It consists of a plastic cap containing an internal metal conductor, which enables hardware-level system recovery and debugging by physically short-circuiting specific pins on the core board. It serves as an essential accessory for in-depth device maintenance and troubleshooting.\n\n1. Remove the multi-function core board from the expansion shield. 2. Place the Jumper Shunt over Pin 1 and Pin 2 on the multi-function core board. 3. Plug the Type-C cable into the multi-function core board and a power supply. 4. Wait for 5 seconds until the LED indicator on the multi-function core board flashes purple, which means the restore is complete. 5. Open the CyberBrick mobile app or the desktop app, reconnect your device, and upload your project.\n\nThe Jumper Shunt is to be used only when resetting the core board. After resetting, be sure to remove the Jumper Shunt and store it properly.\n\nKeep the device out of reach of children to prevent choking hazards.",
